## The two ligatures — this is the single most important instruction

This typeface uses two ligatures. Reproduce each as ONE character. Do NOT expand
them, and do NOT substitute a plain vowel.

  ȣ   U+0223, the ou-ligature. A stacked/closed double loop.
      It is NOT ο+υ, and it is NOT a plain upsilon (which is an open V).
      Writing "ου" or "υ" where the print shows ȣ is an ERROR.
      It routinely carries an accent with NO breathing: ȣ́  ȣ̀  ȣ͂  are all normal
      and must not be "corrected" by adding a breathing.
  ϗ   U+03D7, the kai-ligature. Type ϗ, never καί, never κ, and NEVER ἢ.
      It is a kappa whose tail descends below the baseline. It is not an eta:
      there is no bowl and no breathing mark. Do not let the syntax persuade
      you — "and" and "or" are both grammatical between two nouns, so the
      sentence will read fine either way, and reading fine is not evidence.
      Decide from the strokes alone.
      It often carries a grave and often does not. Copy the mark only if you
      see it on THIS occurrence; adding one that is not there is an ERROR.

